This test file mirrors `StratBridgeParity.cpp`'s harness shape (same table paths, same scenario load through the bridge, same `SeedBridge` failure reporting) and then asserts T-UI-03 clause by clause. Every expected value is read out of a `strat::UiSnapshot` the test obtained from the bridge — the test never recomputes a displayed number from board state.

One thing needs a reviewer's eye and is flagged in the file itself: the exact spelling of `strat::uiCheckSnapshotFidelity`'s result (return-by-value list vs. out-param, and the failure record's member names) is not visible in the sources I was given. I confined that dependency to a single adapter function, `RunSnapshotFidelity`, and used `auto` at the iteration site so the failure struct's *type name* is not restated; if Ui.h spells the result differently, that one function is the whole of the reconciliation.

